<title>UK: UK weighs review of Triplex bid for W.Cook.</title>
<headline>UK weighs review of Triplex bid for W.Cook.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Office of Fair Trading said on Thursday it would invite comments from interested parties into competition issues in the proposed acquisition by Triplex Lloyd Plc of steel firm William Cook Plc.</p>
<p>In a routine announcement, the OFT said representations should be received by December 12.  </p>
<p>Engineering group Triplex Lloyd formally launched its bid, which is in cash and shares, last Friday.</p>
<p>William Cook has pledged to fight it, and has dubbed the bid &quot;financial engineering, wrapped up in spurious industrial logic&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
